SUMMARY:[Maine Agencies] Natural Resources Disaster Relief Assistance Prog
 ram (NRDRAP) applications Open today\, Friday\, August 14
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nMaine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp
 \n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nDACF Home\n→\nAbout DACF\n→\nNewsroom\n→ News
 \nNatural Resources Disaster Relief Assistance Program (NRDRAP) applicatio
 ns Open today\, Friday\, August 14\nAugust 14\, 2026\nThe Maine Department
  of Agriculture\, Conservation and Forestry (DACF) is opening applications
  for the Natural Resources Disaster Relief Assistance Program (NRDRAP) tod
 ay\, Friday\, August 14\, 2026.\nMaine farmers\, forestry businesses\, aqu
 aculture producers\, and other eligible producers who experienced weather-
 related losses in 2023 or 2024 may qualify for financial assistance.\nElig
 ible losses may include crop loss\, aquaculture loss\, standing timber los
 s\, harvested timber loss\, on-farm and forestry infrastructure loss\, and
  bare-ground practices necessary to mitigate land loss.\nApplication perio
 d\n: August 14\, 2026\, through November 6\, 2026.\nApplications will be a
 ccepted through the online portal\n. Paper applications are available upon
  request.\nProducers can prepare now\n. Applicants are encouraged to begin
  gathering documentation\, including:\nOwnership or lease documentation\nP
 arcel ID information\nFSA Farm Number\, if applicable\nTax or business ide
 ntification information\nPhotos or records documenting damage\nOther recor
 ds related to weather-related losses in 2023 and/or 2024 \nDACF will provi
 de technical assistance throughout the application period. Virtual office 
 hours will be held every Friday from 11:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. beginning Aug
 ust 14.\nFor updates\, eligibility information\, and application details\,
  visit\nmaine.gov/dacf/nrdrap\n\, email\nNRDRA.DACF@maine.gov\n\, or call 
 (207) 530-3144.\nBack to Top\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dacf/about/news/news.s
 html?id=13357682
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dacf/about/news/news.shtml?id=13357682
CATEGORIES:Maine Agencies
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
